{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the volume of the solid obtained by rotating the region bounded by the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21326e540d86276bb34b5ee2ec252972ab119155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\dfrac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> and the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> about the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b0605f59cdf11fa141bb55b4b0b376d52293af5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\pi \\text{ cubic units} \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} \\text{ cubic units} \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\text{ cubic units} \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\text{ cubic units} \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\text{ cubic units}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"735\" height=\"34\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We check where the given lines intersect the curve. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca37db8e12fa2d1606cb4edb590caa20a46d742.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = \\frac{1}{x} \\implies x = 1,\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"37\" />\nso the region is bounded vertically by the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. On this interval, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234b330118777aba0bee513e3ade547ebd70d845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is always above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f8c901e38ed39929dda3b04c71e94d3ca028df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is the outer radius, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f8c901e38ed39929dda3b04c71e94d3ca028df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> is the inner radius. Using the washer method of integration with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d403ff11f7c159633466e7157001edcabbc5d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f58d2308e30b77ba8f0e976b56ef68b664d31ba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/405835836f7b9e50965730a68b531458790446f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V = \\pi \\int_{1}^{2} \\left( R^{2} - r^{2} \\right) = \\pi \\int_{1}^{2} \\left[ (1)^{2} - \\left( \\frac{1}{x} \\right)^{2} \\right]  \\, dx = \\pi \\int_{1}^{2} \\left( 1 - \\frac{1}{x^{2}} \\right) \\, dx\\]\" width=\"541\" height=\"53\" />\nEvaluating the integral, we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6232b6271fe2e2a1251497861ace617c76d3caa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi \\left[ x + \\frac{1}{x} \\right]_{1}^{2} = \\pi\\left[ \\left( 2 + \\frac{1}{2} \\right) - \\left(1 + \\frac{1}{1}\\right)\\right] = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\text{ cubic units}}.\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"48\" />\n~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/P